# Git commit author

When creating git commits in this repository, **never** use `cursoragent@cursor.com`, `fcursor@…`, or placeholder names like `Your Name` / `you@example.com`.

Use this identity via environment variables (do **not** run `git config`):

- **Name:** `Moran`
- **Email:** `274483692+mziqudhd92@users.noreply.github.com`  
  (GitHub noreply for `mziqudhd92` — links commits to the repo owner; change only if the user specifies another email)

Example:

```bash
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Moran"
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="274483692+mziqudhd92@users.noreply.github.com"
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Moran"
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="274483692+mziqudhd92@users.noreply.github.com"
git commit -m "your message"
```

Or inline for a single commit:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Moran" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="274483692+mziqudhd92@users.noreply.github.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Moran" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="274483692+mziqudhd92@users.noreply.github.com" \
git commit -m "your message"
```

Do not add a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer unless the user explicitly asks for it.
